# lldpd FHS migration: privsep home/dir /run/lldpd -> /var/run/lldpd.
#
# The daemon itself was always correct: with --localstatedir=/var,
# GNU runstatedir defaults to /var/run, so the privsep chroot
# (/var/run/lldpd), control socket (/var/run/lldpd.socket) and pid
# file (/var/run/lldpd.pid) were never wrong. Only the accounts.d
# fragment named /run/lldpd (home + dir stanza), which additionally
# created the wrong directory at install time. This fragment
# converges the corrected dir and removes the wrong one once empty.
#
# Stale-state policy: pid and control socket are flat daemon-managed
# files under /var/run (persistent by design); lifecycle and stale
# validation belong to the supervising lifecycle, not the layout.
# NOTE (out of scope): lldpd ships no initd/systemd unit in-tree;
# service lifecycle files, if added later, must create
# /var/run/lldpd with _lldpd ownership in both formats.

dir /var/run/lldpd 0755 _lldpd _lldpd
rmdir-if-empty /run/lldpd
